<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>The Short Answer</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Capillary electrophoresis analysis is the step where a bird DNA lab reads, sizes, and interprets fluorescent DNA fragments — separating them inside a hair-thin capillary and converting them into a graph of peaks called an electropherogram. In practice, it is how a lab turns a PCR reaction into a definitive answer: one peak for a male bird, two for a female, and a precise set of sized fragments that forms each bird's unique genetic fingerprint for parentage and identity testing.</p>



