</ul>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="The_Bottom_Line"></span>The Bottom Line<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">CE analysis is the reading step that makes bird DNA testing definitive. It separates and sizes fluorescent fragments with 1–2 bp resolution, then converts them into an electropherogram whose peaks translate directly into biological answers — one peak for a male, two for a female, and a precise profile for parentage and identity.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The same readout powers both of a bird DNA lab's core services, which is why CE has become the universal platform for avian molecular diagnostics. Understanding how it works — and how to read the peaks — is the key to trusting the results.</p>



